// §8c's depth-limit pathological fixture, paired with
// `depth-exceeds-limit.authz` — a chain of 30 distinct namespaces, only
// the last of which grants directly. This invariant's own goal
// (`view(s, o)` where `o: level0`) is what `test/pathological-depth-
// limit.test.ts` checks: the static search finds a real 30-hop witness
// (no depth cap of its own), but self-validation correctly reports
// `mismatch` — the real engine's own `CHECK_MAX_DEPTH` (default 25,
// `src/config/env.ts`) denies it. See that test's own doc comment for
// the full account of why this is a genuine, disclosed static/runtime
// disagreement, not a bug in either component.
invariant deep_chain_view {
  s: user
  o: level0

  goal: view(s, o)
}
